═══ 8/8 REVOCATION (R-C) ═══
[revocation] R-C — junction revocation against a LIVE session (no token refresh)

  signed in as multiStore once; token compared only in memory
  step 1 — before revocation: A1=200 rows · B1=200 rows · stores=[Store A1, Store B1]
  ok   sees both stores' rows (200 + 200)
  step 2 — service role deleted (multiStore, B1). Ground truth: multiStore now holds 1 junction row(s)
  ok   junction ground truth: A1 only
  ok   access token is byte-identical — no refresh occurred between the queries
  step 3 — after revocation, SAME session: A1=200 rows · B1=0 rows · stores=[Store A1]
  ok   B1 rows are gone IMMEDIATELY (0) — revocation is not deferred to token refresh
  ok   A1 rows remain (200) — revocation was surgical, not a blanket lockout
  ok   store list narrowed to A1 only
  step 4 — membership restored (junction back to 6 rows); same session now sees B1=200 rows again
  ok   junction restored to its seeded shape
  ok   re-granting membership is ALSO immediate on the same session

[revocation] R-C PROVEN — revocation and re-grant both take effect immediately, with no token refresh

